      "content": "I understand that seeking medical attention can be daunting, but your symptoms could potentially be significant and warrant a professional assessment. While magnesium supplements can help with relaxation and might alleviate some minor symptoms, they are not a substitute for a medical evaluation. Diving into self-treatment without consulting a healthcare professional could delay the diagnosis and treatment of a potentially serious condition. The best course of action is to see a healthcare provider who can evaluate you, provide you with peace of mind, and offer you the most accurate advice on how to manage your symptoms safely. Until then, keeping yourself hydrated, resting, and considering a gradual, gentle reintegration of exercise when you feel up to it can help support your recovery. Your health should always be the top priority.",
